# CSE450 Translation of Programming Languages
## Bonus Lecture : A Tricky RegEx
---
### Tricky Regular Expression Redux
- **Question:** Give a regular expression that identifies decimal integers that are a multiple of three.
...
- **The trick:** If a number is a multiple of three, its digits add up to a multiple of three.
...
- **Starting off:** Adding any of the digits 0, 3, 6, or 9 does not change whether the sum is a multiple of three.
...
    - `set0  [0369]`
...
- What next?
---
### RegEx (2)
**Definitions:** Three sets of digits will be useful to predefine.
...
{size=25px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
set0  [0369]
set1  [147]
set2  [258]
```
...
These cover all possibilities. `set1` contains digits with remainder 1 modulo 3, and `set2` contains digits with remainder 2.
...
How do we combine these sets?
---
### RegEx (3)
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
...
**The trick:** Whenever `set1` or `set2` appears, other digits must compensate to return the sum to a multiple of three. How can this be done?
...
{size=25px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
{set1}{set2}
{set2}{set1}
{set1}{set1}{set1}
{set2}{set2}{set2}
```
...
We must allow these multiple times, as well as `set0`.
---
### RegEx (4)
**Attempt 1:** Combine alternatives with `set0` between digits.
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
...
{size=25px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
( {set0}+
| {set1}{set0}*{set2}
| {set2}{set0}*{set1}
| {set1}{set0}*{set1}{set0}*{set1}
| {set2}{set0}*{set2}{set0}*{set2}
)+
```
...
Does this solve all of our problems?
---
### RegEx (4)
**Attempt 1:** Combine alternatives with `set0` between digits.
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
{size=25px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
( {set0}+
| {set1}{set0}*{set2}
| {set2}{set0}*{set1}
| {set1}{set0}*{set1}{set0}*{set1}
| {set2}{set0}*{set2}{set0}*{set2}
)+
```
{{color=emp|The `{set0}*` terms allow any number of 0, 3, 6, and 9 digits.}}
Does this solve all of our problems?
---
### RegEx (4)
**Attempt 1:** Combine alternatives with `set0` between digits.
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
{size=25px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
( {set0}+
| {set1}{set0}*{set2}
| {set2}{set0}*{set1}
| {set1}{set0}*{set1}{set0}*{set1}
| {set2}{set0}*{set2}{set0}*{set2}
)+
```
{size=26px} {{color=math|Omit interleaved `{set0}*` terms for now. We’ll restore them later.}}
---
### RegEx (4)
**Attempt 1:** Combine alternatives with `set0` between digits.
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
{size=25px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
( {set0}+
| {set1}{set2}
| {set2}{set1}
| {set1}{set1}{set1}
| {set2}{set2}{set2}
)+
```
{size=26px} {{color=math|Omit interleaved `{set0}*` terms for now. We’ll restore them later.}}
---
### RegEx (4)
**Attempt 1:** Combine alternatives with `set0` between digits.
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
{size=25px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
( {set0}+
| {set1}{set2}
| {set2}{set1}
| {set1}{set1}{set1}
| {set2}{set2}{set2}
)+
```
Does this solve all of our problems?
---
### RegEx (5)
**NO!**
...
We could keep skipping over each multiple of three. Consider this sequence:
{size=28px} `1 1 2 1 2 1 2 1 2 1 2 1 2 1 2 1 2 1 1`
...
This is divisible by three, but our regular expression would not catch it!
...
Can we modify our regular expression to catch this special case?
---
### RegEx (6)
**YES!**
...
{size=27px} We start a skip sequence when we sum to two, then add another two. First, define the starting case:
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
sum2  {set2} | {set1}{set1}
```
...
{size=27px} Now let’s define a single skip:
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
skip  {sum2}{set2}{sum2}
```
...
{size=27px} And allow any number of sequential skips:
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
skip_sequence  {sum2}{set2}({set1}{set2})*{sum2}
```
---
### RegEx (7)
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
sum2           {set2} | {set1}{set1}
skip_sequence  {sum2}{set2}({set1}{set2})*{sum2}
```
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
( {set0}+
| {set1}{set2}
| {set2}{set1}
| {set1}{set1}{set1}
| {set2}{set2}{set2}
| {skip_sequence}
)+
```
---
### RegEx (7)
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
sum2           {set2} | {set1}{set1}
skip_sequence  {sum2}{set2}({set1}{set2})*{sum2}
```
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
( {set0}+
| {set1}{set2}
| {set2}{set1}
| {set1}{set1}{set1}
| {set2}{set2}{set2}
| {skip_sequence}
)+
```
{{color=emp|`{set2}{set2}{set2}` is already covered by `{skip_sequence}`.}}
---
### RegEx (7)
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
sum2           {set2} | {set1}{set1}
skip_sequence  {sum2}{set2}({set1}{set2})*{sum2}
```
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
( {set0}+
| {set1}{set2}
| {set2}{set1}
| {set1}{set1}{set1}
| {skip_sequence}
)+
```
---
### RegEx (7)
`set0 [0369]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set1 [147]` &nbsp;&nbsp; `set2 [258]`
{size=23px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
sum2  {set2} | {set1}{set0}*{set1}
skip_sequence
  {sum2}{set0}*{set2}{set0}*({set1}{set0}*{set2})*{set0}*{sum2}
```
{size=24px, w=1112px, pad=10px} ```
( {set0}+
| {set1}{set0}*{set2}
| {set2}{set0}*{set1}
| {set1}{set0}*{set1}{set0}*{set1}
| {skip_sequence}
)+
```
...
{color=emp, size=40px} **DONE!**
